cd "C:\Users\Aaron Karacas\aura-worker\aura\aura-workers\aura-host"
$subject = @'
A wide panoramic header banner for the "Service & Sacrifice" category of a tattoo website. On the right, a close-up real photograph, framed close from the waist up so the person fills the full height of the photo and the tattoo is large, sharp and easy to read: a woman veteran in her thirties with her hair in a low bun, in a plain olive T-shirt, stands in warm late-afternoon light outside a small house with a porch, her forearm turned toward the camera. On her forearm, a fine-line black-and-grey tattoo of a compass whose north point holds a small date, with a tiny star beside it. On the left, on a deep charcoal background with warm gold light, the words "Service & Sacrifice" written large in strong engraved serif lettering in antique gold, surrounded by original tattoo art of service - a classic anchor, a pair of boots, a dove rising, a lighthouse, a compass and two figures walking side by side, no real military insignia. The art fades softly into the photo through warm light and drifting dust. Proud, respectful and warm, high detail. Only the words "Service & Sacrifice", no other text, no watermark, no logos.
'@
$body = @{ subject=$subject.Trim(); model="gpt-image-2"; width=2048; height=768; exact_size=$true; raw=$true } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress
$j = (RUN ("SHOW_IT " + $body)) | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($j.payload.ok -and $j.payload.id) { "Service & Sacrifice|$($j.payload.id)|$($j.payload.cost_usd)" | Add-Content .\banners-new12.csv -Encoding UTF8; "BANNER Service & Sacrifice - $($j.payload.image_url)  `$$($j.payload.cost_usd)" } else { "BANNER NOT DRAWN: $($j.payload.error)" }
